---
// Home: intro, a small static map (public/img/home-map-splitline.svg, made by pipeline/07_home_map.mjs),
// links to the full map and the methodology, and the (placeholder) signup.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SignupForm from "../components/SignupForm.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const facts = [
  { n: "435", l: "House districts, in all 50 states" },
  { n: "33,585", l: "ZIP code areas, split only where a state line runs through" },
  { n: "0", l: "voter, party or incumbent data used" },
  { n: "420 of 429", l: "multi-seat districts within ±1% of their state's target" },
];
---
<Base
  title="ZIP Code Districts: House districts drawn by unbiased rules, not by politicians"
  description="All 435 U.S. House districts redrawn by joining whole ZIP codes with one fixed rule and no political data. A non-partisan alternative to gerrymandering."
>
  <div class="page">
    <SiteHeader current="home" />
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-text">
          <p class="eyebrow">A non-partisan alternative to gerrymandering</p>
          <h1>What if congressional districts were drawn by unbiased rules, not by politicians?</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            ZIP Code Districts redraws all 435 U.S. House districts by joining whole, neighboring ZIP codes. No voter,
            party or incumbent data is used anywhere. Each state keeps its seats, and every district aims for an equal
            share of its state's population.
          </p>
          <div class="ctas">
            <a class="btn primary" href={`${base}map`}>Explore the map</a>
            <a class="btn" href={`${base}methodology`}>Read the methodology</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-map">
          <a href={`${base}map`} aria-label="Open the full interactive map">
            <img src={`${base}img/home-map-splitline.svg`} width="975" height="610" alt="Map of the United States divided into 435 House districts, each colored to stand apart from its neighbors." />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            Shortest splitline, the most neutral of nine methods. Grey land has no ZIP code because no one lives there.
            <a href={`${base}map`}>Open the full map →</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="facts" aria-label="At a glance">
        <ul>
          {facts.map((f) => <li><b>{f.n}</b><span>{f.l}</span></li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="how" aria-labelledby="how-h">
        <h2 id="how-h">Three simple steps</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <h3>Start with ZIP codes</h3>
            <p>Everyone knows their ZIP code, and ZIP areas weren't drawn for politics. Each ZIP goes whole into one district. Only a state line can divide a ZIP, so your ZIP code tells you who represents you.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Apply one fixed rule</h3>
            <p>The same rule runs in every state, chosen before anyone looks at the results. Shortest splitline, for example, keeps dividing a state with the shortest line that splits its people in the right ratio.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Publish everything</h3>
            <p>The code, the data and the partisan outcomes are all public, so anyone can check the maps, rerun them, or argue with the results.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="more"><a href={`${base}methodology#rules`}>See the full rules →</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
        <h2 id="why-h">The why</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card">
            <b>100 million+</b>
            <p>Americans live in a ZIP code split between congressional districts. Research links split ZIP codes to people knowing and contacting their representative less. <a href={`${base}methodology#prior-work`}>The research →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <b>~25 seats</b>
            <p>That's how far a 2-point shift in the national vote moves the House under shortest splitline. Districts follow voters instead of locking in a result. <a href={`${base}methodology#responsiveness`}>Responsiveness →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <b>Measured after drawing</b>
            <p>Politics-blind maps aren't neutral in outcome. On 2024 results they lean Republican, about as much as today's maps do, because of where voters live. <a href={`${base}methodology#outcomes`}>Partisan outcomes →</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="updates" id="updates" aria-label="Get updates">
        <SignupForm id="home-signup" />
      </section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter signup={false} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* Base sets html, body { height: 100% } for the full-screen map; this page scrolls */
  body { height: auto; min-height: 100%; }
</style>

<style>
  .page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 16px/1.55 var(--font-body);
  }
  main { flex: 1; }
  section {
    max-width: var(--page-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font: 800 clamp(32px, 3.6vw, 46px)/1.08 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lead {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 46px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 22%, transparent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn:hover { border-color: var(--ink); }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--panel); }
  .btn.primary:hover { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }

  .hero-map { margin: 0; }
  .hero-map a { display: block; border-radius: 10px; }
  .hero-map img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    padding: 12px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    transition: box-shadow 0.15s;
  }
  .hero-map a:hover img { box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }

  .facts ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .facts b { display: block; font: 800 28px/1.1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .facts span { display: block; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font: 800 28px/1.15 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font: 700 18px/1.3 var(--font-display); }
  .how, .why { padding-top: 56px; }
  .how ol {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .how li { counter-increment: step; }
  .how li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--panel);
    font: 700 15px/1 var(--font-display);
  }
  .how p, .card p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .more { margin: 20px 0 0; font-weight: 600; }

  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  .card {
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .card b { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font: 800 24px/1.15 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }

  .updates { padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
  .updates :global(.signup) {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; padding-top: 36px; }
    .facts ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .how ol, .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  }
</style>
